diag(pip): Dump the main view for optics that keep the 3DSS path

r__svp_lcd_flat is wired correctly (same entity in UpscalerCompat.h and xrRender_console, registered
in RegisterConsoleVars), so it does reach the shader - and that disproves the lens reflection as the
cause of the halo, because the flat branch would have changed its shape: for RT_FLAT_SCREEN
sample_reflections() switches to a flat normal and skips its vignette modulation, and the specular
is zeroed. A ring that survives all three unchanged is not that layer.

The remaining candidates are drawn for every reticle type, the reticle texture being the first:
mark_texture = s_base.Sample(...) is always blended in, so a circle that is part of the optic's own
screen art would look identical under both types - exactly what was observed. The dump path cannot
settle it either, because it only runs from the publish block, which a thermal optic never reaches
(the engine withholds the lens for it). This adds the missing dump: with r__svp_debug 2 the main
view's combined image is written out while any optic is up, as pip_optics_screen.bmp when the lens
was withheld and pip_optics_lens.bmp when one was rendered.